cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Modalytics in your research, please cite it as below (the article will be added on publication)."
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23991084
title: "Modalytics: an open-source modular multi-modal imaging analysis platform"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Modalytics is an open-source, modular desktop platform for multimodal imaging analysis. It places whole-slide
  images, quantitative phase maps from digital holographic microscopy and other quantitative phase imaging, and
  ordinary microscope images in one micrometre-true space, where they are registered, annotated with vector
  outlines, segmented by neural networks (ONNX Runtime), measured with readable parameter scripts and classified;
  segmentation models and classifiers are trained and validated in the program, and results are written up as
  reports. Analyses are gathered in shareable profiles; the included colonic tissue profile segments glands on DHM
  phase maps and H&E slides and grades dysplasia.
authors:
